Given that the adversary may be using IP 18.66.52.227, it is intended that their code is used to resolve this IP adress to a domain name.
This code is:
PassiveDns
| where ip == "18.66.52.227"
And our answer is then: betterlyrics4u.com

Our next challenge is to check email logs for this domain. It gives another query to run, which initially is just a reconnaissance mission to see what information is contained in the table:
Email
| take 10
We get columns labeled: timestamp, sender, reply_to, recipient, subject, verdict (CLEAN/SUSPICIOUS/BLOCKED), and link.
Which column would be most likely to contain the domain we're looking for?
LINK

The previous query only showed a random 10 emails, hence the "take 10". The next challenge is to look for our suspicious domain in the link column. To do this, we have a query stating:
Email
| where link has "betterlyrics4u.com"
It then asks us how many results we get from this query.
Answer: 13

Which email address was used to send most of the emails that came from that domain? A large portion of these emails are coming from ghostwritersanonymous@protonmail.com.

The next question asks which other email address was used to send these emails, and that answer is wemakebeatz@gmail.com.

We have to find which role was being targeted the most with these emails. It gives us this query to use:
let _targets = Email
| where link has "betterlyrics4u.com"
| distinct recipient;
Employees
| where email_addr in (_targets)
This is setting a table to show emails where the link has the suspicious domain and show only the ones with distinct recipients (so no duplicate emails shown). Then, it takes the information from the Employees table, but only for those employees that had their email address in _targets.
There is a column labeled "Role". Almost everyone in this table has the title of Rapper.

The next question is to determine the other role that was targeted, and the answer is Lead Rapper.

Determine the name of the Lead Rapper - Dwake Audrey.

Find Dwake's IP address - 10.10.0.5.

Now, use a new query to find the subject of the email sent to Dwake. This query is:
Email
| where link has "betterlyrics4u.com"
Sort this table by recipient in alphabetical order to make this a bit easier. From previous questions, I know that Dwake's email address is dwake_audrey@owl-records.com. The immediate next column to the right is the subject line, which is: [EXTERNAL] RE: Need a ghostwriter for your next hit?

Determine the link included in this email: http://betterlyrics4u.com/share/online/published/enter

What is the verdict of this email?
It is listed as CLEAN.

Then, they ask the name that the adversary signed the email with, and that is GhostWriter.

Now, I have to determine if Dwake actually clicked that malicious link.
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where url == "http://betterlyrics4u.com/share/online/published/enter"
| where src_ip == "10.10.0.5"
Unfortunately, there is a result, at 2024-04-15T12:03:12.000Z

What does the Submit button say?
Login to speak with GHOST WRITER.

Did the adversary actually breach Dwake's account?
AuthenticationEvents
| where username == "dwaudrey"
| where src_ip == "18.66.52.227"
There is an event, and the timestamp is: "timestamp": 2024-04-15T13:03:12.000Z

Now, we are asked the result of this attempt: Successful Login
That indicates that Dwake's account was successfully breached.

Now, it is time to see if the adversary exfiltrated any data.
InboundNetworkEvents
| where timestamp between (datetime("2024-04-12T00:00:00") .. datetime("2024-05-01T00:00:00"))
| where url has "dwaudrey" 
| where src_ip has "18.66.52.227"
We run this and we get 10 results.

Now, search in the results to find the name of a ZIP file that was used to gather Dwake's information.
